    <div class="story-card">
        <p>
            <strong>Kinusaiga</strong> is an exquisite Japanese art form that originated in the 1980s. Traditionally, pieces of silk from old kimonos are tucked into finely cut grooves in wood to create intricate, stitchless pictorial tapestries.
        </p>
        <p>
            At <strong>Kinusaiga Art Studio</strong>, we are passionate about keeping this mindful art alive. Every artwork begins with an intricate hand-drawn sketch, transferred onto carved boards, and brought to life with carefully selected silks, brocades, and textured textiles.
        </p>
        <p>
            Our mission is to offer genuine handmade art that is beautiful, distinctive, and accessible for modern Indian homes and special gifting occasions.
        </p>
    </div>

